  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nThe dry cold front passing over the area through the weekend \nwill continue dry and windy conditions on Sunday. Elevated fire \nweather concerns will persist through Sunday. Behind the cold \nfront, Sunday through Monday will be 5-10 degrees cooler than \nnormal. As the front moves out east, Monday will see heightened \nwind gusts mainly over the Upper Treasure Valley and Magic \nValley areas, while very dry conditions persist. Temperatures \nbegin to climb again Tuesday and Wednesday as a Pacific high \npressure system builds into the Great Basin. Wednesday through \nThursday, there is potential for another dry shortwave trough \ndigging across our area from the Pacific coast, but \nconsiderable guidance uncertainty remains. Hot and dry\nconditions will continue through Thursday.",
